 "result_text": "`HttpTransport` no longer uses `Hub`. I removed the `Hub` import and the `hub_cls` attribute from `__init__` in `sentry_sdk/transport.py`. I also removed the `with hub:` wrapper around the worker function in `capture_envelope`. The send now just runs `_send_envelope` and `_flush_client_reports` inside `capture_internal_exceptions()`.\n\n`tests/test_transport.py` passes (45 passed, 32 skipped because eventlet and gevent aren't installed). I didn't run the rest of the test suite.\n\nI also checked non-test code, and nothing else referenced `hub_cls`.\n\nI didn't add anything to carry the caller's scopes into the worker thread. The old `with hub:` wrapper did that, but the send path doesn't appear to need scope state. If you want the scopes carried over anyway, that would be a separate change.",
